 expression of type X collagen (COL10A1) in both humans and mice. It actively coordinates endochondral ossification by mineralising the extracellular matrix, attracting blood vessels via angiogenic signalling, and mediating the transition from cartilage to bone - often by transdifferentiating into an osteoblast rather than undergoing apoptosis.\")\n10188:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35179487\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000743 \"Despite historical descriptions as 'terminally differentiated,' hypertrophic chondrocytes survive and transdifferentiate into osteoblasts. Genetic lineage tracing shows that hypertrophic chondrocytes do not simply undergo apoptosis but cross the cartilage–bone boundary, dedifferentiate into skeletal stem/progenitor cells, and then redifferentiate into osteoblasts and osteocytes. Single-cell RNA-seq further indicates that these chondrocyte-derived SSPCs are a major source of trabecular osteoblasts and marrow adipocytes.\")\n10189:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000743 \"hypertrophic chondrocyte\")\n10190:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000743 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000138 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008187)))\n10191:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000743 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001958))\n10192:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000743 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005693))\n10226:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000746 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000513))\n10234:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000747 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0005005))\n10371:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000762 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000828))\n10380:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000763 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000988 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000049)))\n10405:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000765 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000547))\n10411:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000766 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000738 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000049)))\n10437:SubClassOf(ob